#
# File: Makefile.version
#
# ZangbandTK's own version and the Angband release it is built on.
#
# Both are read out of buildid.h rather than written here as well.  They were
# written in both places, with a comment in each saying it must agree with the
# other, which is a standing invitation to drift -- and the version reaches the
# player from both directions: buildid.h feeds the title screen and the in-game
# copyright, this file feeds Info.plist and so the About panel.  One source, and
# it is the header, because that is the one the C has to have.
#
# Its own file rather than a few lines of Makefile.src, because Makefile.src is
# read by nmake as well, and nmake has no $(shell) -- it stops dead on the first
# one.  Only the makefiles that put a version in front of the player need these:
# Makefile.osx for the About panel, Makefile.std for the tarball name.  Both are
# GNU make, so both can include this.
#

VERSION = $(shell sed -n 's/^\#define VERSION_STRING[[:space:]]*"\(.*\)"/\1/p' buildid.h)
BASE_VERSION = $(shell sed -n 's/^\#define BASE_VERSION_STRING[[:space:]]*"\(.*\)"/\1/p' buildid.h)

COPYRIGHT = ZangbandTK $(VERSION), based on Angband $(BASE_VERSION). (c) 1987-2026 Angband contributors, (c) 1997-2005 Zangband DevTeam, (c) 2026 ZangbandTK contributors
